course: dictionary
lesson: 12794
title: Elapsed time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When time has elapsed, it has passed. Think of a clock that keeps ticking: the time that ticks away is what has elapsed. «Ten minutes elapsed before the bus arrived» means ten minutes went by while you waited.
explain: Elapsed time is the amount of time between a start and an end. If a film starts at 3 o'clock and finishes at 4 o'clock, the elapsed time is one hour. You are finding the gap between two times.
explain: To find elapsed time, count the minutes and hours from the start time to the end time. Count on from the start, or take the start time away from the end time. Always check your answer by counting on again.
fact: «Elapsed» is the past form of the verb «elapse», which means to pass by.
fact: Elapsed time is the time between a start time and an end time.
fact: When you work out elapsed time, you are finding the gap between two times.
fact: Clocks and timers show elapsed time in sport, science experiments and school maths problems.
fact: Words like «time elapsed» and «after an hour had elapsed» tell you that time has passed.
exercise: «Ten minutes elapsed before the bus arrived.» What does elapsed mean here? | Got lost | *Passed | Began | Stopped
exercise: Ella starts her homework at 4:00 and finishes at 4:45. How much time has elapsed? | *45 minutes | 5 minutes | 15 minutes | 4 hours
exercise: «The race was over, and three minutes had elapsed.» Find and copy the word that tells you time went by. | minutes | over | race | *elapsed
test: Sam's swimming lesson starts at 10:15 and ends at 11:00. How much time has elapsed? | 15 minutes | 1 hour 45 minutes | 35 minutes | *45 minutes
test: «Half an hour had elapsed when the rain stopped.» What does elapsed mean? | Had been stolen | *Had passed | Had come back | Had not started
exam: The cake went in the oven at 2:30 and came out at 3:10. How much time had elapsed? | 20 minutes | 50 minutes | *40 minutes | 1 hour
